{"text": "\u2014\noe 4: 3 F or\nWICHIT\nMarch 28, 2019\nVia Electronic Mail\nSynova Cantrell\n\n70961-54551598@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRe: \u2014 Records Request\nDear Synova Cantrell:\n\nPlease be advised that your request for records from the Wichita Police Department (WPD) made\npursuant to the Kansas Open Records Act (KORA) has been forwarded to me for response. You\nhave requested any and all documents related to the murder of Patricia Magers on April 11, 1992\n\nYour request for these records is respectfully denied based upon the following:\n\nThe records you request contain information that pertains an active and on-going criminal\ninvestigation. Pursuant to K.S.A. 45-221(a)(10)(B), a public agency is not required to release\nsuch records if disclosure thereof would interfere with such investigation.\n\nBased upon the foregoing, your KORA request is considered as complete and closed by\nthe City of Wichita.\n\nVery truly yours,\n\n_>ee\n\nCaptain Travis Rakestraw,\nRecords Bureau\n\nPolice Department\nTravis Rakestraw, Captain \u2014 Records Bureau\nCity Hall \u00ab 5\"\" Floor 455 N. Main + Wichita, Kansas 67202\n316.268.4186\nwww.wichita.gov",
